---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import site from "../data/site.json";
const iss = site.repo + "/issues/new";
---
<Base
  title="Add or correct a source"
  eyebrow="Everything here is a file in a public repository"
  dek="There is no login and no moderation queue. The data is JSON on GitHub, and a change to it is an issue or a pull request.">

  <div class="prose" style="max-width:74ch">
    <p>Three things are worth more than anything else you could send:</p>
  </div>

  {/* A ROUTE FOR PEOPLE WHO DO NOT HAVE A GITHUB ACCOUNT.
      Every path on this page was an issue or a pull request, which is a
      developer's idea of how a stranger reports a dead link. The people
      best placed to correct this atlas — an archivist who finds their own
      institution marked «unsurveyed», a researcher who knows a collection
      went behind a paywall last year — will not open an account to say
      so. Rendered only when an address exists, because a contact link
      that goes nowhere is worse than none. */}
  {site.contact && site.contact.email && (
    <div class="one addform" style="margin:22px 0 0;border-left-color:var(--accent)">
      <div class="lab">No account needed</div>
      <p class="cap">David: «so to add sources users need a git account? not
      really feasible». Correct, and this is the way round it. Fill in what you
      know — anything you leave blank is simply left blank — and this writes
      the message for you. <b>Nothing is sent from this page and there is no
      server behind it</b>: the button opens your own mail app with the text
      already in it, or you can copy it and send it however you like.</p>

      <div class="addgrid">
        <label>What is it called
          <input type="text" id="af-name" placeholder="Državni arhiv u Gospiću" /></label>
        <label>Its web address
          <input type="text" id="af-url" placeholder="https://…" /></label>
        <label>Which country or countries
          <input type="text" id="af-cc" placeholder="Croatia" /></label>
        <label>What does it hold
          <input type="text" id="af-what" placeholder="parish registers for Lika-Senj, 1780–1900" /></label>
        <label>What does it cost to look
          <select id="af-access">
            <option value="">I do not know</option>
            <option value="free">Images, free, no account</option>
            <option value="account">Images, free, account needed</option>
            <option value="index">An index only — no images</option>
            <option value="mixed">Partly free, partly paid</option>
            <option value="paid">Images, behind a paywall</option>
            <option value="catalogue">A catalogue entry only — the paper is not photographed</option>
            <option value="onsite">On paper, in the building</option>
          </select></label>
        <label class="addwide">Anything else — how you know, what is wrong, what changed
          <textarea id="af-note" rows="3" placeholder="I am the archivist here and our registers moved to a new portal in March."></textarea></label>
      </div>

      <p class="addbtns">
        <a id="af-send" href="#">Open this in my mail app</a>
        <button type="button" id="af-copy">Copy the message</button>
        <span id="af-said" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
      </p>
      <p class="cap addto">It goes to <b>{site.contact.email}</b>. It will be
      checked against the source before anything changes — that is the whole
      method here, and it applies to a message from a stranger exactly as it
      applies to everything else.</p>
    </div>
  )}

  {site.contact && site.contact.email && (
    <script is:inline define:vars={{ TO: site.contact.email }}>
      (function () {
        /* NO SERVER, NO THIRD PARTY, NO FORM SERVICE. This site is static and
           stores nothing about anybody; posting a stranger's message through
           somebody else's endpoint to avoid asking them to open a mail client
           would trade the one property the whole project is built on for a
           small convenience. So the form composes text, and the reader sends
           it — or copies it, because a mail app is not a safe assumption and
           `mailto:` quietly fails on a machine with none configured. */
        var F = ["af-name", "af-url", "af-cc", "af-what", "af-access", "af-note"];
        var LBL = { "af-name": "Name", "af-url": "Web address",
                    "af-cc": "Country", "af-what": "What it holds",
                    "af-access": "What it costs to look", "af-note": "Notes" };
        function body() {
          var out = [];
          F.forEach(function (id) {
            var el = document.getElementById(id);
            var v = el && el.value ? el.value.trim() : "";
            if (v) out.push(LBL[id] + ": " + v);
          });
          if (!out.length) return "";
          out.push("", "Sent from the Add a source page on Record Atlas.");
          return out.join("\n");
        }
        var send = document.getElementById("af-send");
        var said = document.getElementById("af-said");
        function refresh() {
          var b = body();
          var name = (document.getElementById("af-name") || {}).value || "";
          send.href = "mailto:" + TO +
            "?subject=" + encodeURIComponent("Record Atlas — a source" +
              (name ? ": " + name.trim() : "")) +
            "&body=" + encodeURIComponent(b);
          send.setAttribute("aria-disabled", b ? "false" : "true");
        }
        F.forEach(function (id) {
          var el = document.getElementById(id);
          if (el) { el.addEventListener("input", refresh); el.addEventListener("change", refresh); }
        });
        refresh();
        send.addEventListener("click", function (e) {
          if (!body()) { e.preventDefault(); said.textContent = "Fill in at least one field first."; }
        });
        document.getElementById("af-copy").addEventListener("click", function () {
          var b = body();
          if (!b) { said.textContent = "Fill in at least one field first."; return; }
          var text = "To: " + TO + "\n\n" + b;
          function ok() { said.textContent = "Copied \u2014 paste it into any email."; }
          if (navigator.clipboard && navigator.clipboard.writeText) {
            navigator.clipboard.writeText(text).then(ok, function () { said.textContent = TO; });
          } else {
            /* Older browsers, and any context where the clipboard API is
               blocked: show the address rather than fail silently. */
            said.textContent = TO;
          }
        });
      })();
    </script>
  )}

  <div class="ways">
    <a class="way" href={`${iss}?template=add-source.yml`}>
      <div class="lab">Most useful</div>
      <b>A provider this map does not have</b>
      <span>Especially a national or regional archive outside western Europe. The spine is
      thin wherever this project has not personally researched.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="way" href={`${iss}?template=jurisdiction.yml`}>
      <div class="lab">Rarest</div>
      <b>A region's filing history</b>
      <span>Which archive holds a piece of ground's records, for which years, under which
      regime. This is the hardest thing to find and the thing this map is for.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="way" href={`${iss}?template=dead-link.yml`}>
      <div class="lab">Always welcome</div>
      <b>Something that has changed</b>
      <span>A dead link, a portal that moved, a collection that went from free to paid. A
      directory that lies is worse than no directory.</span>
    </a>
  </div>

  <div class="prose" style="max-width:74ch;margin-top:34px">
    <h3>Or send a pull request</h3>
    <p>The files are small and hand-editable:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>data/providers.json</code> — who holds records, and what access costs</li>
      <li><code>data/regions.json</code> — record regions, their eras, and whose archive each means</li>
      <li><code>data/places.json</code> — places and the volumes that cover them</li>
    </ul>
    <p><code>python3 scripts/check-data.py</code> will tell you whether your change is sound
    before you send it, and the build runs the same check, so nothing lands that fails it.</p>
    <p><b>Every source row must carry a <code>checked</code> date.</b> Not because dates are
    tidy, but because a link with no date is a claim about the present made out of a memory
    of the past.</p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .ways { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
          gap: 14px; margin-top: 22px; }
  .way { display: block; padding: 16px 18px; border: 1px solid var(--rule);
         border-left: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 3px;
         background: var(--panel); text-decoration: none; color: var(--ink); }
  .way:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
  .way b { display: block; font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 18px;
           font-weight: 500; margin: 6px 0 8px; }
  .way span { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.55;
              color: var(--ink-3); }
  code { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12.5px; background: var(--panel-2);
         padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 2px; }
</style>
